/* ---------- THE BRIEF (v28): the desk that solves ----------
   A person says who they are, where they are and what they want. The terminal composes the case memo from its own engines:
   the reading (the tides, the Hammer’s comparables, the room’s temperature), the money (the Navigator’s ledger, the Deal Room’s
   split, the Transformation’s stages), the road (the Navigator’s steps and the playbook’s), the walls (the gates with their
   status, the sanctions file when a counterparty is designated or exposed, the currents’ patterns), the people to call (the Net),
   the calendar (the Season), the whispers, the risks, the next steps, and a draft letter that never leaves the terminal.
   Beside it: the worked cases the research wrote on the same memo (CASES), the compliance files (WALLS), the sources (SOURCES).
   Data: CASES {cases}, WALLS {kandinsky, files}, SOURCES {sources, next} from src/data_net.js (tools/gen_research.py, bundle v28).
   Exposed: window.__BRIEF={compose, parse, open, cases, walls, sources}. */
const BR_WHO=[['collector','A collector'],['specialist','A specialist at a house'],['getter','A business-getter at a house'],['adviser','An art adviser'],['dealer','A dealer'],['executor','An executor or heir'],['family','A family office'],['lender','A lender or a bank'],['insurer','An insurer'],['museum','A museum or a registrar'],['lawyer','A lawyer'],['shipper','A shipper'],['foundation','An artist’s foundation'],['journalist','A journalist']];
